A call through a pointer, a virtual dispatch or a function pointer, has no
callee to read, and the scalar-call replacement refused every such call as
indirect. On the tree this was written against the whole FFI boundary is such
calls, so no mutant ever made the kernel answer something else. The refusal is
lifted: inline asm stays out, since it is not a call, and the intrinsic test
reads the callee only where there is one. An integer return is also taken by
its width, bounded by the two limits the header adds, so that a one-bit
return, which is a bool, can have a replacement of its own. And a replacement
can ask that null be an answer the caller reads, which is where the call is
through a function pointer, the code it names being outside the program, or
where its result reaches a comparison with null in the calling function: a
string's data, an exception's message or a virtual call never answers null,
and replacing those would measure the language's undefined behaviour rather
than the program.
